-- #340: the wilds' nodes on a spacing grid of their own, re-planned.
--
-- The wilds were planned after every other zone on the same spacing grid,
-- by rejection sampling: a rural node by the edge that turned down one wild
-- spot changed every draw after it in that resource's stream. So any change
-- to the rural ring moved the wilds' nodes, though their land and water
-- hadn't changed: 8456 of them at the farms (#290), and on today's world half
-- again the rural nodes would move 11272 of its 14133.
--
-- Now the wilds keep their own grid, with only the existing nodes in it, and
-- start MIN_GAP (12) past the rural edge (`wilds::Land::from`), so they keep
-- their gap from the rural nodes without looking at them. A change to the
-- rural ring moves none of them
-- (`node_spawn::tests::a_change_to_the_rural_ring_moves_no_wild_node`).
--
-- That moves the wild nodes once more, all but the copper and iron veins,
-- high in the ranges, whose streams no rural node ever touched. Nothing
-- outside the wilds moves.
-- So this deletes the rows the plan no longer has, by id, and inserts the
-- new ones, as 20261126_001_rural_farms_nodes.sql did. Nothing a player owns
-- is a node; a node half gathered starts over.
--
-- The rows come from the ignored test `print_node_replan`, and
-- `the_migration_writes_the_default_plan` checks the plan still matches.
--
-- deleted and inserted, 12304 each:
--   clay_bank in wilderness: 393
--   fallen_branches in wilderness: 2986
--   old_growth in wilderness: 5964
--   reed_bed in wilderness: 587
--   rock_outcrop in wilderness: 1977
--   tin_vein in wilderness: 397

